{
  "source": "course-assets/ai-is-math/ai-is-math.mp4",
  "duration": 206.144,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.18,
      "text": "When you type a prompt into chat GPT and receive a coherent response,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.88,
      "end": 6.58,
      "text": "it can feel like the system is thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.28,
      "end": 10.52,
      "text": "Tools like Claude appear to understand context and nuance,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.9,
      "end": 14.54,
      "text": "leading us to wonder what is actually happening behind the interface."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.34,
      "end": 17.74,
      "text": "These systems function by calculating probability,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.36,
      "end": 21.66,
      "text": "analyzing the statistical likelihood of what should happen next."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.36,
      "end": 25.76,
      "text": "This process of predicting outcomes based on specific data"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.76,
      "end": 31.06,
      "text": "traces back to 1654, when mathematicians Blaise Pascal and Pierre de"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.06,
      "end": 33.92,
      "text": "Fremont exchanged letters about the odds in gambling."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.78,
      "end": 38.76,
      "text": "Their work provided the foundation for how we calculate the chance of a future event,"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.12,
      "end": 42.78,
      "text": "a framework that remains central to how modern AI builds an answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.18,
      "end": 47.38,
      "text": "To see how that works, we start with standard probability."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.3,
      "end": 51.86,
      "text": "This applies to scenarios where every possible outcome is equally likely."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.5,
      "end": 53.62,
      "text": "The math is a simple division."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.62,
      "end": 56.68,
      "text": "You count the ways to get the specific result you want,"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.08,
      "end": 59.6,
      "text": "and divide that by the total number of possible outcomes."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.02,
      "end": 62.38,
      "text": "Consider a basic scenario."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.08,
      "end": 63.96,
      "text": "You toss two coins."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.74,
      "end": 68.14,
      "text": "To find the chance both land on heads, we map out the possibilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.08,
      "end": 71.06,
      "text": "There are four equally likely results."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.78,
      "end": 76.96,
      "text": "You could get two heads, a head and a tail, a tail and a head, or two tails."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.72,
      "end": 79.24,
      "text": "Only one matches our goal."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.76,
      "end": 83.02,
      "text": "We divide that successful path by the four total outcomes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.02,
      "end": 86.04,
      "text": "giving a probability of 25%."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.04,
      "end": 89.16,
      "text": "At this stage, without any other information to go on,"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.58,
      "end": 93.12,
      "text": "your odds of seeing two heads are exactly one out of four."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.58,
      "end": 96.58,
      "text": "However, odds are rarely static."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.28,
      "end": 102.04,
      "text": "In mathematics, conditional probability describes how new evidence changes the calculation."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.12,
      "end": 106.32,
      "text": "Imagine we run the toss again, but this time someone peeks."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.84,
      "end": 108.96,
      "text": "They tell you the first coin landed on heads."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.72,
      "end": 112.44,
      "text": "Knowing the first coin is heads changes the landscape."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.44,
      "end": 117.34,
      "text": "Looking back at our original four combinations, some are no longer possible."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.0,
      "end": 123.34,
      "text": "Because the first coin is heads, we can immediately eliminate any outcome starting with tails."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.1,
      "end": 125.66,
      "text": "Those possibilities are ruled out."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.36,
      "end": 129.36,
      "text": "Our total pool of outcomes has shrunk from four to two."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.08,
      "end": 133.94,
      "text": "Out of those two remaining paths, only one results in double heads."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.72,
      "end": 138.32,
      "text": "One divided by two means the probability jumps to 50%."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.32,
      "end": 141.08,
      "text": "The physical state of the coins didn't change,"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.08,
      "end": 142.78,
      "text": "but your knowledge of them did."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.4,
      "end": 147.96,
      "text": "That new information reshaped the odds from 25% to 50%."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.96,
      "end": 153.46,
      "text": "They use the sequence of a conversation to constantly update the probability of what comes next."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.2,
      "end": 158.76,
      "text": "Every word you type in a prompt serves as the evidence that narrows down the possibilities,"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.36,
      "end": 161.62,
      "text": "just like knowing the result of the first coin toss."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.94,
      "end": 168.12,
      "text": "If you ask, what should I name my new dog, and the AI begins its response with,"
    },
    {
      "start": 168.12,
      "end": 172.44,
      "text": "you could name him, those words become the context for the next calculation."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.32,
      "end": 179.1,
      "text": "Based on the words already written, the AI calculates the likelihood for the next word in the sequence."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.78,
      "end": 186.22,
      "text": "It might find a 22% chance for spot, 17% for max, and 14% for buddy."
    },
    {
      "start": 187.46,
      "end": 190.0,
      "text": "Once a word is chosen, it is added to the text."
    },
    {
      "start": 190.66,
      "end": 194.28,
      "text": "This updated string of words becomes the new evidence for the next calculation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 194.28,
      "end": 196.46,
      "text": "and the cycle repeats instantly."
    },
    {
      "start": 198.06,
      "end": 202.24,
      "text": "AI builds answers with probabilities, one prediction at a time."
    }
  ],
